§ `Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child Abuse) Act 2018 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 3 -- child abuse`

-- What was done to the person. s 3 (lines 33-45): child abuse means (a) an act or omission in relation to a person
-- when the person is a minor that is physical abuse or sexual abuse, and (b) psychological abuse (if any) arising out
-- of it, and includes alleged child abuse. Physical abuse does not include an act or omission that is a lawful
-- justification or excuse to battery, or any other lawful exercise of force. Sexual abuse means sexual assault or other
-- sexual misconduct.
DECLARE `Kind of conduct` IS ONE OF
    `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct`
    `physical abuse`
    `force with a lawful justification or excuse, or another lawful exercise of force`
    `psychological abuse alone, not arising out of physical or sexual abuse`
    `other harm, such as neglect`

-- "Minor" is not defined in the Act; it is read as a person under 18 (Age of Majority Act 1977 (Vic) s 3, not
-- deposited; READING in NOTES.md). "Includes alleged child abuse": the facts are the facts the person alleges.
-- A "means" definition: both answers are the text's.
GIVEN `age at the time` IS A NUMBER, `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- it is child abuse` `age at the time` `the conduct` IF
        `age at the time` LESS THAN 18
    AND (    `the conduct` EQUALS `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct`
         OR  `the conduct` EQUALS `physical abuse`)

§§ `ss 5, 6 and 3 -- the NGO and its associated trust`

-- s 5(1) (line 57): "a non-government organisation that is an unincorporated association or body is an NGO". s 3
-- (line 39): NGO "has the meaning given in section 5". s 5(2): no written constitution, fixed membership or other
-- prescribed attribute is needed (none is asked). Read as a definition: both answers are the text's.
GIVEN `it is a non-government organisation` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 -- it is an NGO` `it is a non-government organisation` `it is unincorporated` IF
    `it is a non-government organisation` AND `it is unincorporated`

-- s 6 (lines 63-71): a trust is an associated trust which an NGO controls if any of (a)-(g). s 3 (line 36): control
-- "has the meaning given in section 6", a hand-off to the list, so when no head holds the answer is no (the ruling of
-- 2026-11-05 on delegated definitions, (a)).
GIVEN `a` IS A BOOLEAN, `b` IS A BOOLEAN, `c` IS A BOOLEAN, `d` IS A BOOLEAN, `e` IS A BOOLEAN, `f` IS A BOOLEAN, `g` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 -- the NGO controls the trust` `a` `b` `c` `d` `e` `f` `g` IF
        `a` -- (a) power, directly or indirectly, to control the application of income or distribution of property
    OR  `b` -- (b) power to obtain the beneficial enjoyment of the property or income, with or without consent
    OR  `c` -- (c) power, directly or indirectly, to appoint or remove the trustee or trustees
    OR  `d` -- (d) power, directly or indirectly, to appoint or remove beneficiaries
    OR  `e` -- (e) the trustee is accustomed or obliged, formally or informally, to act on the NGO's directions or wishes
    OR  `f` -- (f) power, directly or indirectly, to determine the outcome of any other decisions about the trust
    OR  `g` -- (g) a member or management member has, under the trust deed, a power of a kind in (a)-(f)

-- s 3 (line 32): "associated trust means a trust which an NGO uses to conduct the NGO's activities and which it
-- controls". A "means" definition.
GIVEN `the NGO uses the trust to conduct its activities` IS A BOOLEAN, `the NGO controls the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- it is an associated trust` `the NGO uses the trust to conduct its activities` `the NGO controls the trust` IF
    `the NGO uses the trust to conduct its activities` AND `the NGO controls the trust`

§§ `s 4 -- application of the Act`

-- s 4(2) (lines 50-53): "This Act applies to an NGO if" (a) a plaintiff commences or wishes to commence a claim against
-- it founded on or arising from child abuse; (b) but for being unincorporated, it would be capable of being sued and
-- found liable for such a claim; (c) it controls one or more associated trusts. An "if": both answers are the text's.
-- s 4(3): whenever the abuse occurred (no date is asked).
GIVEN `the claim is founded on child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an NGO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for being unincorporated it could be sued and found liable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has an associated trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2) -- the Act applies to the NGO` `the claim is founded on child abuse` `it is an NGO` `but for being unincorporated it could be sued and found liable` `it has an associated trust` IF
        `it is an NGO`
    AND `the claim is founded on child abuse`
    AND `but for being unincorporated it could be sued and found liable`
    AND `it has an associated trust`

§§ `ss 7, 8, 13 -- the proper defendant`

-- s 7(3) (line 80): "Unless the court otherwise orders, a nomination of a proper defendant may occur at any time within
-- 120 days after the commencement of the proceeding". Day 120 after commencement is the last day.
GIVEN `the day the proceeding commenced` IS A DATE
      `the court has ordered a different time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day the court allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 7(3) -- the last day for the NGO to nominate a proper defendant` `the day the proceeding commenced` `the court has ordered a different time` `the last day the court allowed` MEANS
    IF `the court has ordered a different time`
    THEN `the last day the court allowed`
    ELSE `plain days after` 120 `the day the proceeding commenced`

-- s 8(1) (lines 85-87): "This section applies to a claim if" (a) the NGO fails to nominate a proper defendant under
-- s 7 within 120 days from the commencement of the proceeding; or (b) the nominee is not an entity capable of being
-- sued or does not have sufficient assets or property to meet any judgment or order. An "if": both answers are the
-- text's. (a) can be known only after day 120 has passed. (a) counts the flat 120 days of its own words even where
-- the court has extended the s 7(3) time (fork line 1). A nomination needs the nominee's consent (s 7(1)), so a
-- "nomination" without it is no nomination.
GIVEN `the Act applies to the NGO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the proceeding commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
      `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the nomination` IS A DATE
      `the nominee is capable of being sued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court would find the nominee lacks sufficient assets to meet a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(1) -- section 8 applies to the claim` `the Act applies to the NGO` `the day the proceeding commenced` `the day of the application` `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent` `the day of the nomination` `the nominee is capable of being sued` `a court would find the nominee lacks sufficient assets to meet a judgment` IF
        `the Act applies to the NGO`
    AND (   (    `the day of the application` `is after` (`plain days after` 120 `the day the proceeding commenced`)
             AND (   (NOT `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent`)
                  OR `the day of the nomination` `is after` (`plain days after` 120 `the day the proceeding commenced`)))
         OR (    `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent`
             AND (   (NOT `the nominee is capable of being sued`)
                  OR `a court would find the nominee lacks sufficient assets to meet a judgment`)))

-- Whom the plaintiff sues.
DECLARE `Defendant` IS ONE OF
    `the NGO itself, in its own name, until a proper defendant is nominated or appointed (s 13)`
    `the nominated entity, as the defendant on behalf of the NGO (s 7(2))`
    `the trustees of the associated trust, as the defendant on behalf of the NGO (s 8(5))`

-- s 7(2) (lines 77-79), s 8(5) (lines 91-93), s 13 (lines 115-118). A court order under s 8(4) names the trustees;
-- otherwise a consented nomination of an entity capable of being sued names the nominee; otherwise, pending either,
-- the proceeding may be commenced or continue against the NGO in its own name. Whether a nominee stays a defendant
-- beside the trustees after an order made under s 8(1)(b) is not said (fork line 2). Where the Act does not apply
-- (s 4(2) fails), it names no one.
GIVEN `the Act applies to the NGO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominee is capable of being sued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ordered the claim to proceed against the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Defendant`
`ss 7, 8, 13 -- the defendant to sue` `the Act applies to the NGO` `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent` `the nominee is capable of being sued` `the court has ordered the claim to proceed against the trustees` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Act applies to the NGO`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 4(2); the ordinary law decides whom to sue)
    ELSE IF `the court has ordered the claim to proceed against the trustees`
         THEN JUST `the trustees of the associated trust, as the defendant on behalf of the NGO (s 8(5))`
         ELSE IF `the NGO has nominated a proper defendant with the nominee's consent` AND `the nominee is capable of being sued`
              THEN JUST `the nominated entity, as the defendant on behalf of the NGO (s 7(2))`
              ELSE JUST `the NGO itself, in its own name, until a proper defendant is nominated or appointed (s 13)`

-- s 13 (lines 115-118): "Pending the nomination ... or the appointment" of a proper defendant, (a) a proceeding for a
-- claim founded on or arising from child abuse may be commenced or continue against an NGO in its own name; (b) a
-- proceeding for a claim may be commenced against an NGO in its own name despite it being unincorporated. "Pending" is
-- a period the text fixes: once a proper defendant is in place the answer is no (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on periods,
-- (a)). Not an NGO the Act applies to: s 4(2)'s "if" fails, and the Act gives no such right (fork line 3 on (b)).
GIVEN `the Act applies to the NGO` IS A BOOLEAN, `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 -- the proceeding may be commenced or continue against the NGO in its own name` `the Act applies to the NGO` `a proper defendant is in place` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Act applies to the NGO`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a proper defendant is in place`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 8(3) (line 89): "the NGO bears the onus of identifying any associated trust" on an application under s 8(2).
-- Outside an application under s 8(2) the section is silent.
GIVEN `section 8 applies to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) -- the NGO bears the onus of identifying its associated trusts` `section 8 applies to the claim` MEANS
    IF `section 8 applies to the claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "For the purposes of an application under subsection (2)")

-- s 7(5) (lines 82-83), s 8(9) (lines 97-98): the nomination or appointment "does not relieve an NGO from any
-- obligations it may have in relation to the conduct of the proceeding, including any interlocutory matters", and for
-- that purpose the NGO is taken to be incorporated. A flat negative. With no proper defendant the NGO is itself the
-- party (s 13) and the subsections are silent.
GIVEN `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7(5), 8(9) -- the NGO keeps its obligations in the conduct of the proceeding` `a proper defendant is in place` MEANS
    IF `a proper defendant is in place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "The nomination ... does not relieve")

§§ `ss 9, 10, 11, 12 -- what follows`

-- s 9(2) (line 103): "Liability of a trustee of an associated trust which is a proper defendant under this section
-- (including liability for costs) is limited to the value of the trust property." No section makes a proper defendant
-- "under this section" (s 9); it is read as a proper defendant under this Act (finding 1). The value is taken at the
-- day it is asked (the Act does not say when; finding 7). One trust: the most recoverable from its trustees is the
-- lesser of the liability and the value.
GIVEN `the judgment and costs` IS A NUMBER, `the value of the trust property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(2) -- the most recoverable from the trustees of one associated trust` `the judgment and costs` `the value of the trust property` MEANS
    min `the judgment and costs` (max 0 `the value of the trust property`)

-- s 9(1) (lines 100-102), s 11 (line 109): despite any Act, law or instrument (including any trust deed) the trustees
-- "may apply any trust property to satisfy any liability incurred in the claim because of being a proper defendant
-- under this Act, including any unpaid judgment debt", the satisfaction is a proper expense for which they may be
-- indemnified out of the trust property, and they are not liable for a breach of trust only because of doing so. A
-- trustee nominated under s 7 is a proper defendant under this Act as much as one appointed under s 8 (finding 2).
GIVEN `the trustees are a proper defendant under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the liability was incurred in the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 9(1), 11 -- the trustees may pay the liability from trust property whatever the trust deed says` `the trustees are a proper defendant under the Act` `the liability was incurred in the claim` MEANS
    IF `the trustees are a proper defendant under the Act` AND `the liability was incurred in the claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "because of being a proper defendant under this Act"; trust law decides the rest)

-- s 10 (line 106): "A proper defendant under section 7 or 8 may rely on any defence or immunity that would have been
-- available to the NGO as a defendant to the claim had the NGO been incorporated." A grant limited in its own wording:
-- outside it, NOTHING.
GIVEN `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN, `the defence would have been available to the NGO had it been incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 -- the proper defendant may rely on the defence` `a proper defendant is in place` `the defence would have been available to the NGO had it been incorporated` MEANS
    IF `a proper defendant is in place` AND `the defence would have been available to the NGO had it been incorporated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: a defence the incorporated NGO would have had; other law decides any other)

-- s 12(1) (line 112): "Any right of an NGO to be indemnified under any policy of insurance in respect of damages awarded
-- in a claim ... founded on or arising from child abuse enures for the benefit of, and extends to, any proper defendant".
-- s 12(2): the NGO keeps its own cover.
GIVEN `the NGO has a right to be indemnified under an insurance policy for such damages` IS A BOOLEAN, `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- the NGO's insurance extends to the proper defendant` `the NGO has a right to be indemnified under an insurance policy for such damages` `a proper defendant is in place` MEANS
    IF `the NGO has a right to be indemnified under an insurance policy for such damages` AND `a proper defendant is in place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "Any right of an NGO to be indemnified"; without one there is nothing to extend)

§§ `Order 85 of the Supreme Court Rules 2025 -- the steps after a nomination`

-- r 85.02(2) (Rules lines 7902-7903): the nomination "shall be filed with the Prothonotary and served on each party ...
-- within 7 days of the nomination being filed". Counted under rr 3.01, 3.04 (lid-dates.l4).
GIVEN `the day the nomination was filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 85.02(2) -- the last day for the NGO to serve its nomination` `the day the nomination was filed` MEANS
    `the last day under the Rules` 7 `the day the nomination was filed`

-- r 85.03 (Rules lines 7906-7910): "unless the court otherwise directs, within 28 days after the service of a
-- nomination on the plaintiff", the plaintiff shall file an amended originating process and statement of claim
-- identifying the proper defendant, and serve it. Service after 4 pm or on a closed day counts from the next open day
-- (r 3.05(2)).
GIVEN `the day the nomination was served on the plaintiff` IS A DATE
      `it was served after 4 pm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has directed a different time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day the court directed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 85.03 -- the last day for the plaintiff to file the amended originating process and statement of claim` `the day the nomination was served on the plaintiff` `it was served after 4 pm` `the court has directed a different time` `the last day the court directed` MEANS
    IF `the court has directed a different time`
    THEN `the last day the court directed`
    ELSE `the last day under the Rules` 28 (`the day taken as served` `the day the nomination was served on the plaintiff` `it was served after 4 pm`)

-- The steps as a rule. Clock: DATE_SERIAL days; the trace starts at the day the proceeding commenced. The NGO may
-- nominate (filing Form 85A, r 85.02(1)) within 120 days (s 7(3)); a nomination starts r 85.02(2) (serve within 7
-- days of filing), and service starts r 85.03 (the plaintiff files the amended process within 28 days after service).
-- No nomination in time: the plaintiff may apply by summons (r 85.04) for an order under s 8. The NGO's choice is
-- neither required nor forbidden, so it is DO with its own HENCE and LEST. Each event carries its own date, from which
-- the next deadline is counted under the Rules (lid-dates.l4); the event's time must be that date's serial.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `the NGO`, `the plaintiff`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `file a nomination of a proper defendant in Form 85A` HAS `the filing day` IS A DATE
    `serve the nomination` HAS `the service day` IS A DATE, `after four` IS A BOOLEAN
    `file the amended originating process and statement of claim`
    `apply by summons for an order that the claim proceed against the trustees of an associated trust`

GIVEN `filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days the NGO has to serve` `filed` MEANS
    `the days from` `filed` `to` (`r 85.02(2) -- the last day for the NGO to serve its nomination` `filed`)

GIVEN `served` IS A DATE, `late in the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days the plaintiff has to amend` `served` `late in the day` MEANS
    `the days from` `served` `to` (`the last day under the Rules` 28 (`the day taken as served` `served` `late in the day`))

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`ss 7, 8 and Order 85 -- nomination, service and amendment` MEANS
    PARTY `the NGO`
    DO    `file a nomination of a proper defendant in Form 85A` `filed`
    WITHIN 120
    HENCE
        PARTY `the NGO`
        MUST  `serve the nomination` `served` `late in the day`
        WITHIN `the days the NGO has to serve` `filed`
        HENCE
            PARTY `the plaintiff`
            MUST  `file the amended originating process and statement of claim`
            WITHIN `the days the plaintiff has to amend` `served` `late in the day`
            LEST  BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "r 85.03: the amended originating process and statement of claim were not filed within 28 days after service of the nomination"
        LEST  BREACH BY `the NGO` BECAUSE "r 85.02(2): the nomination was not served within 7 days of being filed"
    LEST
        PARTY `the plaintiff`
        MAY   `apply by summons for an order that the claim proceed against the trustees of an associated trust`

§§ `Read with: Wrongs Act 1958 s 88(ba), s 93`

-- Wrongs Act s 88 (lines 2238-2241): "relevant organisation means an entity (other than the State) organised for some
-- end, purpose or work that exercises care, supervision or authority over children ... and is ... (ba) an NGO within
-- the meaning of the Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child Abuse) Act 2018 which is capable of being sued
-- in accordance with that Act". "Capable of being sued in accordance with that Act" is read as: this Act applies to the
-- NGO (s 4(2)), since s 13 then lets it be sued in its own name (fork line 4). s 93 (line 2302): Part XIII applies to
-- abuse on or after 1 July 2017 (No. 12/2017 in operation that day); before it, NOTHING. Para (ba) only: the other
-- heads (such as a nomination under Wrongs Act s 92) are in the Wrongs Act's own encoding.
GIVEN `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE
      `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it exercises care, supervision or authority over children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act applies to the NGO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Wrongs Act s 88(ba), s 93 -- the NGO is a relevant organisation` `the day of the abuse` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it exercises care, supervision or authority over children` `the Act applies to the NGO` MEANS
    IF `the day of the abuse` `is after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2017)
    THEN IF `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` AND `it exercises care, supervision or authority over children` AND `the Act applies to the NGO`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: Wrongs Act s 93; the common law governs earlier abuse)

§§ `Read with: Limitation of Actions Act 1958 ss 27O, 27P, 27Q`

-- s 27O(1) (lines 683-688): Division 5 applies to an action founded on the death or personal injury of a person
-- resulting from an act or omission in relation to the person when a minor that is physical or sexual abuse (and
-- psychological abuse arising out of it). s 27P(1) (lines 712-714): such an action, unless it arises under Part III of
-- the Wrongs Act 1958 (a death claim by dependants), "may be brought at any time". s 27Q (lines 717-721): a Part III
-- action, within 3 years from the day it is discoverable: no, not at any time. "Physical abuse" is not defined in
-- the Limitation Act; lawful force (excluded by this Act's s 3) is read as outside it (READING in NOTES.md). Outside
-- Division 5: NOTHING (the other Divisions govern).
GIVEN `the action is for death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age at the time` IS A NUMBER
      `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`
      `the action arises under Part III of the Wrongs Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Limitation Act ss 27O, 27P -- the action may be brought at any time` `the action is for death or personal injury` `age at the time` `the conduct` `the action arises under Part III of the Wrongs Act` MEANS
    IF `the action is for death or personal injury` AND `s 3 -- it is child abuse` `age at the time` `the conduct`
    THEN IF `the action arises under Part III of the Wrongs Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 27O(1); Divisions 2 and 3 govern other actions)
